    {
      "id": "P008",
      "kind": "finding",
      "heading": "Recommendation, not adjudication",
      "text": "In its offer, the prosecution said the NBI investigation led to complaints alleging three grave-threats counts and one inciting-to-sedition count. The chair later confined Lotoc's answer to whether the NBI believed it had prima facie evidence sufficient to file complaints, expressly not whether an offense had been committed. Lotoc described the NBI result as a recommendation submitted to the Justice Department for evaluation.",
      "citations": [
        {
          "segment_id": "S00136",
          "start_seconds": 2018.48,
