    {
      "id": "P010",
      "kind": "finding",
      "heading": "The document challenge",
      "text": "On cross-examination, the defense questioned the Justice Department's initial case-build-up requirement, receiving dates, docket markings, and later-added affidavits. Counsel asked whether a date discrepancy demonstrated tampering, but the chair sustained the objection. When the questions moved to a Justice Department document outside Lotoc's competence, the chair said a DOJ witness would be needed. The session produced no finding that any document had been altered or tampered with.",
      "citations": [
